-- title:
--   Places over j₀ on X_H(M) as ± H-orbits of M-torsion
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be an algebraically closed field with decidable equality, $M$ a nonzero natural number invertible in $K$ (i.e. $(M : K) \neq 0$), $H$ a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, $j_0 \in K$, and $E_0$ a Weierstrass curve over $K$ which is elliptic and has $j$-invariant $j_0$. Let $F =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC K (CohCarrier.GammaH M H)` be the subfield of the Laurent series field $K((q))$ generated over $K$ by the coefficientwise reductions of ratios $p_f/p_g$ of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of equal weight on $\Gamma_H(M) = \{\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M) : \gamma \bmod M \text{ has unit entry in } H\}$, and let $x \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is `jqModC K`, the reduction to $K$ of $q^{-1}\,(E_4^3\eta^{-24})$. Let $S$ be a finite set of places of $F$ over $K$ (valuation subrings of $F$ containing $K$, proper, with principal ideal domain as valuation ring) whose members are exactly the places $Q$ with $\operatorname{ord}_Q(x - j_0) > 0$, where $\operatorname{ord}_Q$ is minus the logarithm of the associated adic valuation. Write $\mathcal{X}$ for the type of subsets $s$ of the affine point set $E_0(K)$ for which there exists $P \in E_0(K)$ of exact additive order $M$ with $s = \{(u \bmod M).\mathrm{val}\cdot P : u \in H \sqcup \langle -1\rangle\}$, the subgroup generated by $H$ and $-1$. The assertion is that there is a map $f : \mathcal{X} \to \{\text{places of } F \text{ over } K\}$ such that: $f$ takes values in $S$; every $Q \in S$ is of the form $f s$; for $s, s' \in \mathcal{X}$ one has $f s = f s'$ if and only if there is a variable change $\gamma$ over $K$ with $\gamma \bullet E_0 = E_0$ such that each $T \in s$ has some $T' \in s'$ with `Point.vcInvFun` $\gamma$ applied to $T$ heterogeneously equal to $T'$; and for every $s$, $\operatorname{ord}_{f s}(x - j_0)$ equals the cardinality of the fibre $\{s' : f s' = f s\}$, viewed as an integer.
--
--   This is the modular interpretation of the fibre of $j \colon X_H(M)_K \to X(1)_K$ over a point $j_0$ when $M$ is invertible in the algebraically closed field $K$: the places of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(M)$ lying over $j_0$ correspond to the orbits, under the automorphisms of the Weierstrass model $E_0$, of $\pm H$-orbits of points of exact order $M$ on $E_0$, and the order of vanishing of $x - j_0$ at such a place is the size of the corresponding orbit, i.e. the ramification index. It is used in the census of such places in characteristics $2$ and $3$ and in the computation of $\operatorname{ord}$ of $x - j_0$ at places of the function field of $X_1$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_orbitMap_torsionOrbit_places_qExpFunctionFieldC_gammaH.lean

